      "description": "Single-celled organisms abundant in marine environments, from shallow coastal waters to the deep ocean.",
      "value": "Their shells, or tests, are preserved in marine sediments and can be used to reconstruct past environmental conditions.",
      "oxygen_isotopes": {
        "ratio": "The ratio of oxygen-18 to oxygen-16 is particularly informative.",
        "sensitivity": "This ratio is sensitive to changes in temperature and the isotopic composition of seawater, which itself is influenced by global climate patterns."
      }
