    "description": "The theory posits that cosmic rays can ionize molecules in the atmosphere, leading to the formation of aerosols. These aerosols can act as cloud condensation nuclei, promoting the formation of clouds. Clouds, in turn, can have both warming and cooling effects on the Earth's climate, depending on their type and altitude. High, thin clouds tend to warm the Earth by trapping heat, while low, thick clouds have a cooling effect by reflecting sunlight back into space.",
